{-| `Std.Ai.Dataset` — typed training and evaluation data: load it, clean it,
split it, check it, and freeze it into a content-addressed version.

    import Std.Ai.Dataset as Dataset exposing (Instruction, Split(..))
    import Std.Ai.Dataset.Scrub as Scrub

    support : Dataset.Dataset Instruction
    support =
        Dataset.fromJsonl Dataset.instructionCodec "data/support.jsonl"
            |> Dataset.scrub (Scrub.forInstruction Scrub.defaults)
            |> Dataset.dedupeBy .prompt

    freezeSupport : Task Error (Dataset.Version Instruction)
    freezeSupport =
        support
            |> Dataset.split Dataset.defaultSplit .prompt
            |> Dataset.freeze (Dataset.folder "data/versions" "support") Dataset.instructionCodec

A `Dataset row` is a description. Nothing is read until you freeze it,
validate it or ask for its rows, and a JSONL file is read in chunks of lines,
so a large file never sits in memory (`fromCsv` and `fromStore` read their
source whole, because a CSV field can span lines and a store is one query).

A split puts each row in `Train`, `Eval` or `Test` by a SHA-256 hash of the
row's key and the split's seed, not by a random draw. The same row is in the
same split in every version, so the eval rows never leak into training when
new data arrives.

A frozen `Version` is canonical JSONL (each line `{"row":…,"split":…}`, object
keys sorted, no insignificant white space, `\n` endings) named by the SHA-256
of its bytes, and a manifest that records the sources, the steps, the row
counts per split, the scrub report, the schema of the row codec, the creation
time and an optional consent basis and retention period. The same rows frozen
twice give the same digest. A training job takes a `Version`, never a live
`Dataset`, so its lineage is fixed by the type.

A file that cannot be read, a line that is not JSON or a row that does not
decode is the typed `Std.Ai.Failure.DatasetInvalid` (`InvalidInput`), which
names the file and the line, never the row's text. A version whose bytes do
not match its digest is `ChecksumMismatch`. See `docs/ai/dataset.md`.
-}

